    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d728">

                <pb facs="0835" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/448: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-03T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1919,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your Number 6 February 27, 8 P.M.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d728-f1"/></p>
                <p>Your telegram was only received by Department late the afternoon of March 1 and
                    Congress adjourns at noon tomorrow. The Department regrets that owing to
                    shortness of time and the tremendous <pb facs="0836" n="734" xml:id="pg734"/>
                    press of business before Congress during the last few hours of this session,
                    including appropriation bills of vital importance, it has not been possible to
                    submit the amended Treaty for ratification. To have done so at this time might
                    have had a prejudicial result on the negotiations.</p>
                <p>It is very probable that there will be a special session of Congress in June and
                    in that case Congressional action upon the Treaty can be obtained at that
                    time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
